  "note": "Pins spec/domain/brick.md RATIFIED v1 (Xuan 2026-08-31) \u2014 the FIRST domain-family slice; file lives at vectors/domain/, not vectors/fueling/. engine=null: brick_eligibility.dart is app-internal, not a published interface; defining the published predicate (and its seam) is part of the brick-transition bundle. EXPECTED-RED on two vectors by ruling: r5-* (skipped legs are linkable in code today \u2014 D-007). BUNDLE: brick-transition. Gate identities are part of the contract (min-legs / max-legs / ineligible-leg): a rejection for the wrong reason is a failure. ORACLE CONVENTIONS: candidateIds preserve day order; create-time validation order is subset-check then count (no spec order given; no emitted case fails two gates at once so order is unchallenged). NOT COVERED: R7 delete-brick=ungroup (stateful behaviour \u2014 app-side widget/integration test, not a pure-predicate vector); R8 positional transition identity (a cross-function SEAM, covered by the bundle's producer-shaped seam test per qa 8b12b9d, not assertable in one engine); past/future-day legs (input shape carries no date \u2014 Q-BR1); direct brick extension (Q-BR2). One characterization tripwire pins the open Q-BR1 done/verified case.",
